{"id":1372,"date":"2020-11-27T15:19:31","date_gmt":"2020-11-27T23:19:31","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1372"},"modified":"2023-08-21T08:40:40","modified_gmt":"2023-08-21T15:40:40","slug":"program-the-soccer-bot","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-soccer-bot\/","title":{"rendered":"Program the Soccer Bot"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221662af68d\" name=\"6a221662af68d\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Briefing video<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This video goes over how to program the Soccer Bot. Don&#8217;t forget to go through the rest of the lesson![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=&#8221;https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=vkuOJALGBBI&#8221; align=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221662af7c2\" name=\"6a221662af7c2\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What does it do?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The Soccer Bot can be used with a remote control! It can move forward, backward, right, and left to play soccer.<\/p>\n<p>This is what the Soccer Bot&#8217;s pseudocode looks something like:<\/p>\n<ul>\n<li>If the up button on the remote control is pressed, move forward.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if down is pressed, move backward.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if left is pressed, turn left.<\/li>\n<li>Else, if right is pressed, turn right.<\/li>\n<li>Else, stop.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221662af822\" name=\"6a221662af822\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Setup<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]The first thing you need to do is include the Smart Inventor library at the top of your code. Next, in void setup(), include your motors and remote control.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n    SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221662af876\" name=\"6a221662af876\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Reading the remote control<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Create a\u00a0variable\u00a0to read the\u00a0remote control\u00a0and store information about the last button that was pressed. You want this information to be read continuously, so make sure it&#8217;s in\u00a0void loop().<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt;\r\n\r\nvoid setup() {\r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();\r\n    SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();\r\n}\r\n \r\nvoid loop() {\r\n    int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221662af8c6\" name=\"6a221662af8c6\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The up button<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Next up: the main section of the code! Use an\u00a0if statement\u00a0to check if the\u00a0remote control&#8217;s up button\u00a0was pressed. If it was, the\u00a0motors\u00a0will turn to move the Soccer Bot forward.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n    int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData(); \r\n    if(keyData == KEY_U)\r\n    {\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ Move forward\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 50);\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221662afa06\" name=\"6a221662afa06\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>The down, left, and right buttons<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]If you want to add more\u00a0buttons, you can use\u00a0else if statements\u00a0in your code. Your code will run through these only if the past if or else if statements were false. For example, if the only button that was pressed was the left button, your Soccer Bot&#8217;s motors will move in the same direction to turn left.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">void loop() {\r\n    int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();\r\n \r\n    if(keyData == KEY_U)\r\n    {\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ Move forwards\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 50);\r\n    }\r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_D)\r\n    {\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ Move backwards\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, 50);\r\n    }\r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_L)\r\n    {\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ Turn left\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, 50);\r\n    }\r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_R)\r\n    {\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ Turn right\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 50);\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221662afa85\" name=\"6a221662afa85\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>No buttons<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]What if you want your Soccer Bot to slow down? You can add an\u00a0else statement\u00a0to the end of your code to bring your Soccer Bot to a slow stop when no\u00a0buttons\u00a0are pressed.<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt; \r\n\r\nvoid setup() {    \r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();    \r\n    SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();\r\n} \r\n\r\nvoid loop() {    \r\n    int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();     \r\n\r\n    if(keyData == KEY_U)    \r\n    {        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ Move forwards        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 50);    \r\n    }    \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_D)    \r\n    {        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ Move backwards        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, 50);    \r\n    }    \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_L)    \r\n    {        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ Turn left        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, 50);    \r\n    }    \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_R)    \r\n    {        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ Turn right        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 50);    \r\n    }\r\n    else\r\n    {\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0); \/\/ Stop\r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, LOOSE, 0);\r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a221662afad9\" name=\"6a221662afad9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 8<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Final code<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]This is what your final code should look like:<\/p>\n<pre class=\"EnlighterJSRAW\" data-enlighter-language=\"cpp\">#include &lt;SmartInventor.h&gt; \r\n\r\nvoid setup() \r\n{    \r\n    SmartInventor.DCMotorUse();    \r\n    SmartInventor.TVRemoconUse();\r\n} \r\n\r\nvoid loop() \r\n{    \r\n    int keyData = SmartInventor.TVRemoconData();     \r\n    \r\n    if(keyData == KEY_U)    \r\n    {        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ Move forwards        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 50);    \r\n    }    \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_D)    \r\n    {        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ Move backwards        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, 50);    \r\n    }    \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_L)    \r\n    {        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CCW, 50); \/\/ Turn left        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CCW, 50);    \r\n    }    \r\n    else if(keyData == KEY_R)    \r\n    {        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, CW, 50); \/\/ Turn right        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, CW, 50);    \r\n    }    \r\n    else    \r\n    {        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M1, LOOSE, 0); \/\/ Stop        \r\n        SmartInventor.DCMotor(M2, LOOSE, 0);    \r\n    }\r\n}<\/pre>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 9 Briefing video [vc_column_text]This video goes over how to program the Soccer Bot. Don't forget to go through the rest of the lesson![\/vc_column_text][vc_video link=\"https:\/\/www.youtube.com\/watch?v=vkuOJALGBBI\" align=\"center\"] [\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column] Step 10&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/program-the-soccer-bot\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1740,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":true,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":802,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1760,1777,1808,1793,1913,2058,1907,1915,423,626,1533,1438,853,144,59,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2163,2218,2173,2123,2122,2172,2171,2210],"class_list":["post-1372","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-arduino","lesson-tag-computer-science","lesson-tag-electronics","lesson-tag-fundamentals","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-robotics","lesson-tag-rokit-smart","lesson-tag-soccer-bot","module-soccer","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1372","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":4,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1372\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":6618,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1372\/revisions\/6618"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1740"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1372"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1372"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1372"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}